source: tests/journey/cli.rs
expression: "run(pace().arg(\"--help\"))?"
---
success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
pace: a local-first command-line time tracker for work and daily life

Usage: pace [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  begin   Begin an entry; a running entry ends at the new start [alias: b]
  hold    Note an interruption of the running entry [alias: h]
  pause   Take a planned break from the running entry [alias: p]
  resume  Go on after a hold or a pause [alias: r]
  catch   Write a distraction down without breaking off [alias: c]
  end     End the running entry [alias: e]
  now     Show what is running, held or paused [alias: n]
  config  Look at pace's configuration
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <FILE>  Read the global configuration from FILE [env: PACE_CONFIG]
      --home <DIR>     Keep pace's data in DIR [env: PACE_HOME]
      --project <KEY>  The project to work on, instead of discovering it [env: PACE_PROJECT]
      --plain          Plain output: no colour, no symbols
  -h, --help           Print help
  -V, --version        Print version

----- stderr -----
